WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:13,620
Why not methylated B vitamins for cancer?

00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:17,820
Okay, so methyl groups are essential for life.

00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:19,340
We need methyl groups.

00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:26,220
So a methyl group is a carbon with three hydrogens, and it can bind to, you could use it to bind

00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:33,580
to different nutrients, to get them exogenously, you also get methyl groups through your foods.

00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:39,940
So most people that are eating good diets are getting plenty of methyl groups, but taking

00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:45,760
exogenous methyl groups, taking exogenous methyl groups in B vitamins, you're taking methyl

00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:50,980
cobalamine, which is methyl B12 for methyl tetrahedral folate, which is a methyl methyl

00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:51,980
folate.

00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:56,220
Now most natural doctors will say, that's the best type of folate, that's the best type of

00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,220
B12.

00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:00,580
Well, maybe, maybe not.

00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:03,780
Well, certainly maybe not, if you have cancer.

00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:09,860
The reason is that what are the major things that methyl groups do is they silence genes,

00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:15,100
so they turn off genes, which you need to have genes turned off at different times.

00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:21,180
However, one of your greatest way to kill cancer, if you have cancer, is through a pathway

00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:30,660
called your intrinsic, meaning inside the cell, capsaic pathway, or intrinsic apoptotic pathway.

00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:38,220
So the intrinsic apoptotic pathway is stimulated by, when a cancer cell is going through rapid

00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:42,660
replication, it stimulates what are called your tumor suppressor genes.

00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,660
Everybody has them.

00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:47,340
You have lots of different tumor suppressor gene families.

00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:52,860
The bronca gene is probably the most well known by lay people.

00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:56,940
So the bronca genes are a tumor suppressor gene that turns out in breast cancer and can

00:01:56,940 --> 00:02:02,180
help kill the breast cancer, so you never know you even have breast cancer, because it's

00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:07,420
dead before it gets to a size of you ever discovering that.

00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:12,620
Now if you take a bunch of methyl groups, you can turn those genes off, so you can hinder

00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,900
your body's ability to kill cancer.

00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:23,660
So my rule is, if you have cancer, you're not taking methyl groups, take other forms of

00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:25,460
B12 and other forms of folate.

